            <div xml:id="d63">

                <pb facs="0181" n="65" xml:id="pg65"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.515/11.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Reinsch to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 113.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Peking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-02-12">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 12, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my despatch No. 89 of January
                    26th, with which I transmitted, for the information of the Department, a
                    translation of the Currency Law then understood to have received the approval of
                    the President, I have the honor to send you herewith the translation of the
                    National Currency Law, together with the accompanying detailed regulations for
                    its enforcement, in the form in which it was promulgated on February 7th. It
                    will be observed that in its final form the Law (Article 5) established for the
                    subsidiary silver coins different weights from those prescribed in the earlier
                    draft. I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paul S. Reinsch</hi></signed>.</closer>


                <xi:include href="d63-a1.xml" xpointer="d63-a1"/>
            </div>
